("deleted material, e.g., by typing `I$}'.");error();
incr(align_state);
}

@ Here is where we clear the parameters that are supposed to revert to their
default values after every paragraph and when internal vertical mode is entered.

@p void normal_paragraph()
{if (looseness!=0) eq_word_define(int_base+looseness_code, 0);
if (hang_indent!=0) eq_word_define(dimen_base+hang_indent_code, 0);
if (hang_after!=1) eq_word_define(int_base+hang_after_code, 1);
if (par_shape_ptr!=null) eq_define(par_shape_loc, shape_ref, null);
}

@ Now let's turn to the question of how \.{\\hbox} is treated. We actually
need to consider also a slightly larger context, since constructions like
`\.{\\setbox3=}\penalty0\.{\\hbox...}' and
`\.{\\leaders}\penalty0\.{\\hbox...}' and
`\.{\\lower3.8pt\\hbox...}'
are supposed to invoke quite
different actions after the box has been packaged. Conversely,
constructions like `\.{\\setbox3=}' can be followed by a variety of
different kinds of boxes, and we would like to encode such things in an
efficient way.

In other words, there are two problems: to represent the context of a box,
and to represent its type.

The first problem is solved by putting a ``context code'' on the |save_stack|,
just below the two entries that give the dimensions produced by |scan_spec|.
The context code is either a (signed) shift amount, or it is a large
integer | >= box_flag|, where |box_flag==@t$2^{30}$@>|. Codes |box_flag| through
|box_flag+255| represent `\.{\\setbox0}' through `\.{\\setbox255}';
codes |box_flag+256| through |box_flag+511| represent `\.{\\global\\setbox0}'
through `\.{\\global\\setbox255}';
code |box_flag+512| represents `\.{\\shipout}'; and codes |box_flag+513|
through |box_flag+515| represent `\.{\\leaders}', `\.{\\cleaders}',
and `\.{\\xleaders}'.

The second problem is solved by giving the command code |make_box| to all
control sequences that produce a box, and by using the following |chr_code|
values to distinguish between them: |box_code|, |copy_code|, |last_box_code|,
|vsplit_code|, |vtop_code|, |vtop_code+vmode|, and |vtop_code+hmode|, where
the latter two are used to denote \.{\\vbox} and \.{\\hbox}, respectively.

@p
static constexpr auto box_flag=010000000000; /*context code for `\.{\\setbox0}'*/
static constexpr auto ship_out_flag=box_flag+512; /*context code for `\.{\\shipout}'*/
static constexpr auto leader_flag=box_flag+513; /*context code for `\.{\\leaders}'*/
static constexpr auto box_code=0; /*|chr_code| for `\.{\\box}'*/
static constexpr auto copy_code=1; /*|chr_code| for `\.{\\copy}'*/
static constexpr auto last_box_code=2; /*|chr_code| for `\.{\\lastbox}'*/
static constexpr auto vsplit_code=3; /*|chr_code| for `\.{\\vsplit}'*/
static constexpr auto vtop_code=4; /*|chr_code| for `\.{\\vtop}'*/

Put_each_of_TeXs_primitives_into_the_hash_table = [&]() {
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"moveleft"/*)pool_string*/, hmove, 1);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"moveright"/*)pool_string*/, hmove, 0);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"raise"/*)pool_string*/, vmove, 1);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"lower"/*)pool_string*/, vmove, 0);

primitive(/*pool_string(*/"box"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, box_code);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"copy"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, copy_code);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"lastbox"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, last_box_code);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"vsplit"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, vsplit_code);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"vtop"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, vtop_code);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"vbox"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, vtop_code+vmode);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"hbox"/*)pool_string*/, make_box, vtop_code+hmode);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"shipout"/*)pool_string*/, leader_ship, a_leaders-1); /*|ship_out_flag==leader_flag-1|*/
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"leaders"/*)pool_string*/, leader_ship, a_leaders);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"cleaders"/*)pool_string*/, leader_ship, c_leaders);
primitive(/*pool_string(*/"xleaders"/*)pool_string*/, leader_ship, x_leaders);
}};

Cases_of_print_cmd_chr_for_symbolic_printing_of_primitives = [&](quarterword cmd, halfword chr_code) { switch(cmd) {
case hmove: if (chr_code==1) print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"moveleft"/*)pool_string*/);
    else print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"moveright"/*)pool_string*/);break;
case vmove: if (chr_code==1) print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"raise"/*)pool_string*/);
    else print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"lower"/*)pool_string*/);break;
case make_box: switch (chr_code) {
  case box_code: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"box"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  case copy_code: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"copy"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  case last_box_code: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"lastbox"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  case vsplit_code: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"vsplit"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  case vtop_code: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"vtop"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  case vtop_code+vmode: print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"vbox"/*)pool_string*/);break;
  default:print_esc(/*pool_string(*/"hbox"/*)pool_string*/);
  } break;
